    "P satisfies Assumption 3",
    "delta <= 0.15"
   ],
   "tuning": [],
   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "thm:GeneralBoundFC",
    "number": "Theorem 4",
    "quote": "Let $\\nu\\in \\cM_m$, where $\\cM_m$ is defined by (\\ref{BM:General}), and assume that $\\cP$ satisfies Assumption~\\ref{assumption}; any algorithm that is $\\delta$-PAC on $\\cM_m$ satisfies, for $\\delta \\leq 0.15$, \\[\\bE_\\nu[\\tau]\\geq \\left[\\sum_{a\\in \\mathcal{S}^*_m}\\frac{1}{\\K(\\nu_{a},\\nu_{[m+1]})} + \\sum_{a\\notin \\mathcal{S}^*_m}\\frac{1}{\\K(\\nu_{a},\\nu_{[m]})}\\right]\\log\\left(\\frac{1}{2.4\\delta}\\right).\\]"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Applies to all delta-PAC algorithms on M_m."
  },
